{"id":"NCT06134232","title":"Metastatic Castrate-Resistant Prostate Cancer Subjects Treated With PROVENGE® + One Infusion of Sipuleucel-T","official":"An Open -Label, Multicenter Study of Subjects With Metastatic Castrate-Resistant Prostate Cancer Treated With PROVENGE ® and Boosted With A Single Infusion of Sipuleucel-T to Measure Immune Response","summary":"A multicenter, open-label, prospective study to investigate immune boost response changes in patients with metastatic castrate-resistant prostate cancer (mCRPC).","conditions":["Metastatic Castration-Resistant Prostate Cancer (mCRPC)"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Sipuleucel-T Injection"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\nFor a subject to be eligible for participation in this study, all of the following criteria must be satisfied:\n\n1. Potential subjects are men aged ≥18 years who are clinically indicated for treatment with PROVENGE® (asymptomatic or minimally symptomatic metastatic castrate-resistant \\[hormone refractory\\] prostate cancer).\n2. Have qualified for on-label PROVENGE® infusion\n3. Have received all 3 infusions of PROVENGE® prior to randomization\n4. Written informed consent provided prior to the initiation of study procedures\n5. Estimated life expectancy ≥12 months\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\nA subject will not be eligible for participation in this study if any of the following criteria apply.\n\n1. Men who are not clinically indicated for treatment with PROVENGE® (asymptomatic or minimally symptomatic metastatic castrate-resistant \\[hormone refractory\\] prostate cancer).\n2. Need for systemic chronic immunosuppressive therapy, including antitumor necrosis factor alpha monoclonal antibodies, glucocorticoids, systemic steroids, blood products, GM-CSF or granulocyte colony-stimulating factor (G-CSF), any vaccinations, or experimental and investigational therapies (see Section 6.3.1)\n3. Uncontrolled, concurrent illness, including, but not limited to the following: ongoing or active infection (bacterial, viral, or fungal), or psychiatric illness that would limit compliance with study requirements, as well as any condition that would preclude a subject from completing PROVENGE® or sipuleucel-T treatment.\n4. On experimental or investigational therapy.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"MALE","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":400,"start":"2023-10-02","pcd":"2031-12-31","upd":"2025-08-27","sponsor":"Dendreon","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Margaret Warner-Lubin · 2064588358 · ProvONE@dendreon.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Arizona Urology Specialists","city":"Tuscon","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85741","s":"R","lat":null,"lon":null,"c":"Kalpesh Patel, MD · 520 618 1010 · kpatel@arizonauro.com"},{"f":"City of Hope - National Medical Center","city":"Duarte","pr":"California","zip":"91010","s":"R","lat":34.1394,"lon":-117.9773,"c":"Tanya Dorff Principal Investigator, MD · 626-218-6585 · mtuano@coh.org"},{"f":"Urology Associates of Central California Medical Group","city":"Fresno","pr":"California","zip":"93720","s":"R","lat":36.7477,"lon":-119.7724,"c":"William Schiff, MD · 559 321 2800 · drschiff@urologyassociates.net"},{"f":"Unio Health Partners - Genesis Research, LLC","city":"San Diego","pr":"California","zip":"92123","s":"R","lat":32.7157,"lon":-117.1647,"c":"Paul Dato, MD · 858 279 7050 ext. 2676 · Paul.Dato@UnioHP.com"},{"f":"Colorado Urology","city":"Lakewood","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80228","s":"R","lat":39.7047,"lon":-105.0814,"c":"David Cahn, MD · 303-996-9649 · dcahn@coloradouro.com"},{"f":"Advanced Urology Institute","city":"Daytona Beach","pr":"Florida","zip":"32114","s":"R","lat":29.2108,"lon":-81.0228,"c":"Evan Fynes, MD · 386 239 8500 · Evan.fynes@auihealth.com"},{"f":"Advanced Urology Institute","city":"Largo","pr":"Florida","zip":"33771","s":"R","lat":27.9098,"lon":-82.7884,"c":"Matthew Truesdale, MD · 813 245 3782 · matthew.truesdale@auihealth.com"},{"f":"Advanced Urology Institute","city":"Ocala